<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · British Isles</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of the Magonsaete</h1><p class="st-meta">650 CE – 740 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A small Anglian sub-kingdom on the Welsh border in Herefordshire and Shropshire, ruled by Merewalh's dynasty under Mercia.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Magonsaete, perhaps named after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magnis">Magnis</a> (Kenchester), emerged in the mid 7th century in the borderlands west of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/river-severn">Severn</a>. Their first known ruler was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/merewalh">Merewalh</a>, whom later tradition made a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/penda-of-mercia">Penda</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-mercia">Kingdom of Mercia</a>, though this is uncertain.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/merewalh">Merewalh's</a> family was noted for piety: his daughter <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mildburh">Mildburh</a> founded the abbey of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/much-wenlock">Much Wenlock</a>, and other children became saints. A bishopric at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hereford">Hereford</a> served the people. The rulers were sub-kings under Mercian overlordship, and the population included many <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britons-celtic-people">Britons</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The dynasty disappears from record in the 8th century, and the territory was absorbed directly into <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-mercia">Mercia</a>. Its outline survived as the diocese of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hereford">Hereford</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 650 CE – 740 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">British Isles</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:72.64%;width:1.79%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>650 CE – 740 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Merewalh, Merchelm, Mildfrith</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Old English</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/united-kingdom">United Kingdom</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Magonsaete, Westerna</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=695&amp;focus=kingdom-of-the-magonsaete" aria-label="Kingdom of the Magonsaete on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4608 294 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of the Magonsaete lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4962 619h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4928 550h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M4928 550h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day United Kingdom. <a href="/atlas?year=695&amp;focus=kingdom-of-the-magonsaete">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
